WEBVTT

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:38.740
Abenobashi is a shopping and entertainment area in Osaka.

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:41.820
It's apparently been 50 years since the shopping arcade was built here...

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:44.930
...but I've never heard any rumors of supernatural phenomena until now.

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:46.670
According to the person who designed it...

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:50.370
...the shopping arcade is as scientifically sound as it can be.

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:51.840
So, goblins...

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:53.460
...great evil lords...

00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:55.460
...giant robots...

00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:57.340
...and members of their own families cosplaying...

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:00.800
...much less a busty, naughty lady with glasses...

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:03.810
...should absolutely not appear without good reason.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:07.020
Huh? Then how in the world did this all happen?

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:08.490
Oh, speaking of which...

00:02:08.490 --> 00:02:10.690
...that person who said he designed the shopping arcade...

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:13.070
I feel like I've seen him before somewhere.

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:24.300
Looks like this isn't the right town either.

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:27.310
You and I have both become completely different people.

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:32.340
The night fog transformed me into an adult woman.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:36.080
Being an adult is too sad, baby.

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:40.420
Sasshi, you mean to go, don't you?

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:43.360
In the end, we're just migrating birds.

00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:46.680
To not be able to settle in one town for long is our fate.

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:48.680
Sasshi...

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:51.950
Good grief, what a cruel town.

00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:57.060
Even a cute guy like Spot here has a pitch-black shadow.

00:02:57.370 --> 00:02:59.170
Come here, Spot. Spot, Spot.

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:09.980
Arumi, run!

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:12.670
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:15.090
Let's pull out of here!

00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:16.920
What?

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:19.050
You're Arumi's mom!

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:22.930
Oh, my! Hello, there! How's your mom doing?

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:23.550
Oh...

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:26.360
But this is no time to be saying that.

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:29.520
If the flatfeet catch us, it'll be a disgrace to the Pelican Family.

00:03:34.710 --> 00:03:35.810
Hey, not me!

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:38.320
Oh, wai... Sasshi!

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:40.640
Arumi's the one in the pelican family!

00:03:40.850 --> 00:03:42.550
My family's the turtle!

00:03:42.550 --> 00:03:43.840
Quit making a racket!

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:48.920
Damn, they got away.

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:51.760
Excuse me, who were they?

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:53.400
The Pelican Family.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:55.580
The gang that's got control of this shopping arcade.

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:57.600
Gang?

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:01.470
Wow, I guess our shop has a pretty extensive business.

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:06.220
Y'all were ambushed by the law, you say?

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:09.340
It isn't even like you.

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:11.430
I am sorry.

00:04:11.910 --> 00:04:15.470
So? You delivered our terms, I hope?

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:18.740
To the legendary sniper Rugolgo, that is?

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:20.490
Actually...

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:23.240
Ha! Can't you even run a child's errand successfully?

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:24.930
I am sorry.

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:26.130
Well, that's all right.

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:28.530
He's an honest-to-goodness pro.

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:30.240
He'll show up here.

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:34.660
Ladies, don't you miss your chance to see Rugolgo in action.

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:36.470
Yes, sir.

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:37.340
Mister.

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:38.310
Yes?!

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:42.480
I haven't see you around before. Is this your first time here?

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:44.670
Uh, well...

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:49.640
You'd better not be one of the law's stooges.

00:04:49.950 --> 00:04:51.640
No! No, I'm not!

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:09.950
He's no spy!

00:05:11.270 --> 00:05:12.810
Yeah, yeah, yeah!

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:16.330
This is the man we have been waiting for! It's Rugolgo!

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:21.450
You have done well to come here, my friend.

00:05:21.450 --> 00:05:23.470
No, well, that is...

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:24.450
You must be joking.

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:25.920
No, there's no mistake about it.

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:29.580
Snipers are people who just show up out of nowhere.

00:05:30.690 --> 00:05:34.480
Hence the legend surrounding the legendary man.

00:05:35.030 --> 00:05:38.020
Thank you for making the long trip, my son.

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:48.210
Excuse me.

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:50.160
What is this?

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:53.540
Save the private chatter for your own time, Arumi Police.

00:05:53.780 --> 00:05:56.320
I'm asking you what this police business is about!

00:05:56.320 --> 00:05:58.820
I'd like to introduce you to your partners.

00:05:58.820 --> 00:06:00.670
Listen to what I'm saying!

00:06:05.660 --> 00:06:06.090
A!

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:07.850
Be!

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:11.430
No!

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:13.600
Abeno Angels!

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:17.070
Don't make me do something so stupid!

00:06:19.910 --> 00:06:23.110
She's got a slightly violent streak, but she's energetic.

00:06:23.450 --> 00:06:25.110
Nice enthusiasm too.

00:06:26.050 --> 00:06:28.360
Abeno Angels, presently heading out on our mission, sir!

00:06:28.980 --> 00:06:32.680
Very good. Danger is dangerous. Be plenty careful.

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:35.080
Hold on a second there!

00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:37.080
Excuse me...

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:39.020
Where are you going?!

00:06:39.190 --> 00:06:40.760
Where do you think?

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:43.030
We're going to round up the Pelican Family.

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:46.390
They're still dealing in those repulsive goods!

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:47.630
How horrifying!

00:06:48.070 --> 00:06:50.840
What repulsive goods?

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:54.850
Well, you should probably know about it ahead of time as well.

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:57.240
Yes, you should definitely know about it.

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:00.550
I agree, you ought to know about it.

00:07:02.680 --> 00:07:04.860
Hurry up and tell me! It's bugging me now!

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:09.150
The street price is 900 yen for a plate of three.

00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:12.490
Escargot bourguignon.

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:13.700
With toast.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:15.700
Just what I'd expect from you, Rugolgo.

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:17.330
You know what the deal is.

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:18.420
Aw, quit it.

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:21.040
This is the source of our capital.

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:23.510
Thanks to the snail prohibition...

00:07:23.510 --> 00:07:25.420
...the price for these guys has gone through the roof.

00:07:25.940 --> 00:07:29.110
But business has been getting a little tough to conduct lately.

00:07:29.110 --> 00:07:33.980
That's where you, the legendary sniper, Rugolgo, come in.

00:07:34.420 --> 00:07:36.380
He's the target.

00:07:36.380 --> 00:07:38.220
Chief of the Abenobashi Police.

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:40.020
Hey, it's Grandpa!

00:07:40.490 --> 00:07:43.160
I get it. Grandpa and I are buddies...

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:45.860
...so all I gotta do is ask him to let you guys cheat a little.

00:07:46.290 --> 00:07:50.650
Like hell I'd ask the legendary sniper to do something that an errand boy could do!

00:07:51.670 --> 00:07:54.150
Then what? Do I gotta write a letter or something?

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:58.160
You moron, you're a sniper, so of course you're gonna shoot him with your rifle!

00:07:58.310 --> 00:08:00.000
Rifle?

00:08:00.340 --> 00:08:01.740
That's just wrong!

00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:02.940
There's nothing wrong with that!

00:08:02.940 --> 00:08:05.410
It is wrong! That's murder!

00:08:06.810 --> 00:08:08.080
Murder?

00:08:08.350 --> 00:08:10.720
How dare you make such a scandalous suggestion?!

00:08:10.820 --> 00:08:14.220
Scandalous, nothing. People die if you shoot 'em with a rifle!

00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:18.390
Roger, roger. I most certainly accept the job, mariachi.

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:20.390
Who the hell're you?!

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:24.900
Oh, a real sniper must not stand out.

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:26.960
You're mega flashy.

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:31.400
Non, non, non. You, monsieur, are an imposter.

00:08:31.970 --> 00:08:33.270
An imposter?!

00:08:33.270 --> 00:08:38.040
Oui. I am the legendary sniper, Rugolgo. Enchanté.

00:08:39.480 --> 00:08:41.660
You tricked us?!

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:45.390
Tricked you?! You guys got it all wrong on your own!

00:08:45.850 --> 00:08:48.360
Oh, I know, he's gotta be the imposter!

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:49.850
Yeah, he's definitely suspicious!

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:51.660
He's supposed to be a legendary sniper...

00:08:51.660 --> 00:08:54.860
...but he's got an M16A assault rifle. That's not right!

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:57.170
Listen to me real good, Ma'am.

00:08:57.170 --> 00:09:02.180
The lightweight bullets fired from this rifle's .223 caliber barrel...

00:09:02.180 --> 00:09:04.700
...have a high initial velocity of 1,000 m/s...

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:08.380
...but its practical range is only about 400 meters.

00:09:08.380 --> 00:09:12.400
There is no way a pro would use this thing for sniping!

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:15.840
Wow!

00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:17.950
You shouldn't be impressed by that!

00:09:19.520 --> 00:09:21.910
As a pro, I am very partial to this gun.

00:09:22.260 --> 00:09:25.360
I see. That's the way you should be if you're a pro.

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:26.460
This rifle...

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:29.860
...is just mega cool! Amore mio!

00:09:29.860 --> 00:09:31.250
Moron.

00:09:31.570 --> 00:09:33.260
Just which one's the real one?!

00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:38.550
Be patient. We'll find out which one's real soon enough.

00:09:41.510 --> 00:09:44.480
You first. Use this gun to hit that can.

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:45.260
Whoa!

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:49.210
It's a M2006M revolver made by Mateba!

00:09:49.580 --> 00:09:51.620
Talk about hard core.

00:09:51.620 --> 00:09:53.380
Listen to me real good, Ma'am.

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:56.860
This gun's made so you can easily remove this barrel...

00:09:56.860 --> 00:09:58.520
...and switch it with another one.

00:09:58.790 --> 00:10:01.560
And by having the hammer hit the bottom bullet in the cylinder...

00:10:01.560 --> 00:10:02.820
...it greatly reduces the recoil when you fire the gun.

00:10:02.930 --> 00:10:06.890
That's what's special about this gun.

00:10:07.800 --> 00:10:09.200
See? Ain't it great?

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:10.670
Yeah, for real!

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:14.540
Never mind that, just hurry up and shoot!

00:10:16.540 --> 00:10:17.570
I hit it!

00:10:17.980 --> 00:10:20.820
Wow! That was awesome! I hit it, I hit it! See? See? See?

00:10:20.820 --> 00:10:21.970
Brilliant!

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:23.950
You're going to accept that?!

00:10:23.950 --> 00:10:26.020
He did an amazing job hitting the target from that stance.

00:10:26.290 --> 00:10:27.410
You're next.

00:10:32.290 --> 00:10:33.010
Moron.

00:10:52.110 --> 00:10:54.600
I believe the winner is me.

00:10:55.620 --> 00:10:56.480
That was perfect!

00:10:56.480 --> 00:10:57.710
That's ridiculous!

00:10:58.250 --> 00:11:00.360
Even if his opponent was just a single can...

00:11:00.360 --> 00:11:02.420
...he thoroughly and mercilessly subdued it.

00:11:02.420 --> 00:11:04.320
That's the spirit of a pro.

00:11:05.590 --> 00:11:09.720
I will acknowledge him as the true legendary Rugolgo.

00:11:11.130 --> 00:11:13.270
We have no use for an imposter legend.

00:11:13.630 --> 00:11:14.800
You're kidding me!

00:11:14.800 --> 00:11:17.170
I haven't done anything!

00:11:19.640 --> 00:11:21.110
He shot me for real.

00:11:26.410 --> 00:11:29.410
What the heck? My legs are so short.

00:11:29.780 --> 00:11:31.290
I look like a dork.

00:11:39.730 --> 00:11:40.830
The problem is...

00:11:40.830 --> 00:11:44.390
...we don't know where in that building Big Boss is hiding out.

00:11:44.630 --> 00:11:47.800
This Boss is just gonna turn out to be Grandpa again, right?

00:11:48.170 --> 00:11:50.230
I've already begun to see the pattern here.

00:11:50.670 --> 00:11:52.170
You must not underestimate him!

00:11:52.170 --> 00:11:54.150
Big Boss is the greatest villain in this town!

00:11:54.940 --> 00:11:59.490
I see, so the villains in this town make money by selling snails.

00:11:59.880 --> 00:12:01.880
What a stupid and peaceful town.

00:12:01.880 --> 00:12:03.580
Couldn't they at least sell stag beetles?

00:12:03.580 --> 00:12:06.150
This isn't good. We'll stand out if we're dressed like this.

00:12:06.150 --> 00:12:07.590
Standing out my butt!

00:12:07.590 --> 00:12:10.880
Then why did we come out here dressed like such idiots to begin with?!

00:12:11.530 --> 00:12:14.100
Mune-mune Police, I expected something like this might come up...

00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:16.360
...so I came prepared with a costume to infiltrate the place.

00:12:16.360 --> 00:12:17.100
Good.

00:12:17.100 --> 00:12:20.090
There's something a little wrong with you guys! Think about it!

00:12:20.230 --> 00:12:22.740
If you thought something like this might come up...

00:12:22.740 --> 00:12:24.510
...you should put that outfit on from the start and...

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:26.310
That was very prudent of you, Sayaka Police.

00:12:26.310 --> 00:12:27.680
Let's begin the operation immediately!

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:29.300
Listen to what I'm saying!

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:30.510
Huh?

00:12:30.510 --> 00:12:31.550
What?

00:12:31.550 --> 00:12:33.780
Don't tell me we're gonna change right here?!

00:12:33.780 --> 00:12:34.950
What?! Stop!

00:12:34.950 --> 00:12:39.120
Even grade school kids these days would not strip in a place like this, ladies!

00:12:39.120 --> 00:12:40.320
Oh, wait!

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:41.900
No! Perverts!

00:12:43.720 --> 00:12:44.450
Hey...

00:12:45.330 --> 00:12:46.370
Hey, hey!

00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:48.950
Hello? Don't just ignore me!

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:51.290
Pitiful fool.

00:12:51.430 --> 00:12:55.060
It means you're finished once you've been turned into a comic relief character like that.

00:12:55.600 --> 00:12:58.710
No one will take you seriously in this shopping arcade now.

00:12:59.340 --> 00:13:00.460
Not ever.

00:13:00.710 --> 00:13:02.380
Who're you calling a comic relief character?!

00:13:02.380 --> 00:13:03.410
I'm gonna hit you for that!

00:13:03.410 --> 00:13:04.310
I...

00:13:04.310 --> 00:13:05.750
Have short legs.

00:13:05.750 --> 00:13:07.850
Come on, isn't Rugolgo a comic relief character too?

00:13:07.850 --> 00:13:11.680
Setting a bomb on that can was a gag routine, wasn't it?

00:13:19.030 --> 00:13:20.080
You are?

00:13:20.860 --> 00:13:24.170
How would you like to hear a song tonight?

00:13:24.170 --> 00:13:25.180
A song?

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:26.720
You're gonna sing?

00:13:27.270 --> 00:13:28.590
Would that displease you?

00:13:30.540 --> 00:13:32.440
She looks so cool!

00:13:33.170 --> 00:13:34.280
I'm so not cool.

00:13:34.280 --> 00:13:42.080
For a sweet dream, a rouge ribbon...

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:48.020
...encrusted with pearls...

00:13:50.220 --> 00:13:58.100
Cheap dreams... Please, not for me...

00:13:58.100 --> 00:14:03.630
...aim for my heart...

00:13:59.630 --> 00:14:01.150
Arumi...

00:14:03.840 --> 00:14:07.140
Arumi's turned into such a cool-looking, mature girl...

00:14:06.810 --> 00:14:09.740
Not silk dresses...

00:14:07.140 --> 00:14:09.740
...of course she wouldn't take a comic relief character like me seriously.

00:14:09.980 --> 00:14:11.250
Fine then, see if I care.

00:14:10.810 --> 00:14:13.810
Not diamonds...

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:14.750
That man is not Big Boss.

00:14:14.880 --> 00:14:17.780
Not bouquets of roses...

00:14:15.520 --> 00:14:17.470
He is certain to be hiding here somewhere.

00:14:18.020 --> 00:14:19.990
I checked all the rooms on the second floor.

00:14:18.850 --> 00:14:21.780
Not glass shoes...

00:14:19.990 --> 00:14:21.780
The only place left is up these stairs.

00:14:22.820 --> 00:14:29.990
Presents won't sway me...

00:14:26.430 --> 00:14:28.500
Bon appetite.

00:14:37.640 --> 00:14:38.730
Huh? We didn't get hit!

00:14:40.070 --> 00:14:42.980
This is my so-called "legend" or legend.

00:14:43.740 --> 00:14:45.110
I will deliver the finishing blow now.

00:14:49.550 --> 00:14:51.020
Rugolgo's been shot!

00:14:54.390 --> 00:14:55.540
Such short legs.

00:14:56.060 --> 00:14:58.080
Police! You're all under arrest!

00:14:58.360 --> 00:14:59.620
Give up quietly!

00:15:00.130 --> 00:15:03.510
Give up quietly?! Who d'you think you're talking to?!

00:15:08.770 --> 00:15:10.380
I'll hold them off here!

00:15:10.370 --> 00:15:11.410
Go after Big Boss!

00:15:11.410 --> 00:15:12.930
All right! Thanks!

00:15:21.250 --> 00:15:24.320
Oh, Sasshi, where have you gone?!

00:15:34.300 --> 00:15:35.760
I've finally found you!

00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:37.200
Hands in the air, Big Boss!

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:41.300
Rough and rude as ever, aren't you?

00:15:42.140 --> 00:15:44.100
It wasn't even locked.

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:48.640
I'm placing you under arrest!

00:15:48.740 --> 00:15:50.010
What will you do after you arrest me?

00:15:51.110 --> 00:15:52.580
Why do you have to leave?

00:15:53.050 --> 00:15:56.020
I've been waiting for you all this time.

00:15:56.020 --> 00:15:57.310
All this time!

00:15:57.550 --> 00:15:59.790
It is impossible to do things over.

00:15:59.790 --> 00:16:00.540
What things?

00:16:01.190 --> 00:16:02.160
Everything.

00:16:02.160 --> 00:16:03.210
Everything?

00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:06.290
Just like the movement of this planet...

00:16:06.290 --> 00:16:09.160
...the fate of humans cannot be altered.

00:16:09.160 --> 00:16:10.130
Forever...

00:16:10.430 --> 00:16:12.430
And that is what you mean by everything?

00:16:12.430 --> 00:16:14.370
Everything there is the universe as you see it?

00:16:14.370 --> 00:16:19.040
And my heart will pine for you in this hellishly hollow town...

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:21.610
...forced to wander aimlessly forever.

00:16:21.610 --> 00:16:23.410
That is everything there is of me.

00:16:23.880 --> 00:16:24.430
Mune...

00:16:25.610 --> 00:16:30.420
If I could share even a small part of the burden of your fate with you, I would.

00:16:31.120 --> 00:16:33.850
But I already have my hands full dealing with my own fate. I'm sorry.

00:16:33.850 --> 00:16:34.590
You can't!

00:16:35.860 --> 00:16:37.720
Go downstairs and catch Masayuki.

00:16:37.890 --> 00:16:38.470
No!

00:16:39.090 --> 00:16:41.200
You are the only one I am after!

00:16:41.200 --> 00:16:42.890
No! Don't go!

00:16:50.870 --> 00:16:52.030
Abe-san...

00:16:57.980 --> 00:16:59.660
What short legs.

00:17:00.280 --> 00:17:03.940
I guess it doesn't hurt when you become a comic relief character.

00:17:05.220 --> 00:17:06.520
It does too hurt!

00:17:06.950 --> 00:17:09.390
What happened? Why're you so cute-looking now?

00:17:12.030 --> 00:17:14.890
Adults have all sorts of circumstances to deal with!

00:17:15.400 --> 00:17:18.350
You just look funny, even if you're trying to act cool.

00:17:18.350 --> 00:17:19.390
Leave it!

00:17:26.170 --> 00:17:28.270
Say, have you seen Sasshi anywhere?

00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:31.170
I'm not in the mood for any of that right now!

00:17:31.580 --> 00:17:34.100
That was the perfect spot for observing the stars.

00:17:35.020 --> 00:17:38.530
It was a mistake to teach Masayuki the snail business.

00:17:40.420 --> 00:17:42.020
This place is just too serious.

00:17:42.020 --> 00:17:44.180
I'm moving to a more easygoing world!

00:17:44.390 --> 00:17:45.790
Wait a minute!

00:17:46.430 --> 00:17:48.790
Do us just one, just one favor!

00:17:48.790 --> 00:17:50.790
We want to get back to our original world.

00:17:52.230 --> 00:17:54.170
Didn't you get the goblins to take care of that?

00:17:54.370 --> 00:17:57.200
I'm asking you 'cause the goblins aren't reliable!

00:17:57.540 --> 00:18:00.610
They always cut corners and every time we think we've gotten home...

00:18:00.610 --> 00:18:02.580
...we've been transported to someplace weird again.

00:18:02.980 --> 00:18:03.940
Transported?

00:18:04.150 --> 00:18:06.550
Well, yeah, and each one's weirder than the last.

00:18:07.210 --> 00:18:09.880
Then the god Vishnu was summoned correctly.

00:18:10.150 --> 00:18:11.850
If you're changing worlds...

00:18:11.850 --> 00:18:15.160
... his power is manifesting itself, even though the target location may be slightly off.

00:18:15.160 --> 00:18:19.250
If corners were cut, you guys would have remained in that world.

00:18:19.890 --> 00:18:21.920
Then why can't we get back home?

00:18:22.430 --> 00:18:24.760
Because you guys don't want to go back home.

00:18:25.270 --> 00:18:27.030
That's ridiculous! We do...

00:18:27.230 --> 00:18:29.260
What? Could Sasshi be...

00:18:29.570 --> 00:18:30.420
Oh, him.

00:18:31.640 --> 00:18:34.730
For some reason, he has a more than casual connection with me.

00:18:35.480 --> 00:18:37.380
But I can't have you guys getting attached to me because of that.

00:18:42.020 --> 00:18:44.210
Wow, talk about an ugly Sasshi.

00:18:45.090 --> 00:18:47.710
You guys definitely have quite a connection going there.

00:18:48.720 --> 00:18:52.660
I can't stand having you guys scampering underfoot anymore!

00:18:53.030 --> 00:18:54.520
Hurry up and go home!

00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:57.390
I'm personally making the magic circle for you!

00:18:57.800 --> 00:19:00.770
Even the Emperor doesn't get to experience this all that often.

00:19:01.740 --> 00:19:04.230
If it was someone at the ministry level, I'd never do it for them!

00:19:04.640 --> 00:19:05.940
Mister, what're ya mad about?

00:19:05.940 --> 00:19:08.380
Well, of course he's in a sour mood.

00:19:08.380 --> 00:19:10.280
He's got those short legs now.

00:19:10.380 --> 00:19:11.500
But that goes for you too.

00:19:12.280 --> 00:19:13.500
There, it's done.

00:19:13.880 --> 00:19:15.020
You know the rest, right?

00:19:15.020 --> 00:19:16.550
Man, thanks, Mister.

00:19:17.150 --> 00:19:18.550
Thank you.

00:19:22.120 --> 00:19:23.090
What?

00:19:23.090 --> 00:19:24.390
No, nothing.

00:19:24.530 --> 00:19:26.890
Okay, shall we go back to our Abenobashi now?

00:19:27.390 --> 00:19:28.360
This time...

00:19:30.130 --> 00:19:31.150
Say, Sasshi?

00:19:32.130 --> 00:19:34.400
Don't you think it's a little too bad?

00:19:34.740 --> 00:19:35.600
About what?

00:19:35.600 --> 00:19:38.370
Well, rather than go back to our own town...

00:19:38.370 --> 00:19:41.710
...it'd be sort of more fun if we got to go to all sorts of other worlds.

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:44.640
Don't you kinda think so?

00:19:44.850 --> 00:19:46.640
Oh, you think so?

00:19:47.110 --> 00:19:50.280
Actually, I was thinking it was fun too.

00:19:50.850 --> 00:19:53.420
'Cause, you know, they've got my favorite things no matter where we go.

00:19:54.050 --> 00:19:56.820
So, even when we're chanting the spell to go home...

00:19:57.020 --> 00:20:00.920
...all I can think about is what's gonna show up next...

00:20:00.920 --> 00:20:02.960
...and I get so excited each and every time.

00:20:03.030 --> 00:20:04.900
It's just so fun!

00:20:05.570 --> 00:20:06.530
Sasshi.

00:20:07.130 --> 00:20:12.400
I've had a feeling that this might be the case for a while...

00:20:12.840 --> 00:20:15.240
...but I wasn't quite sure about it.

00:20:16.910 --> 00:20:20.050
But ya know, it's crystal clear to me now.

00:20:20.050 --> 00:20:21.820
You're a moron!

00:20:21.850 --> 00:20:22.650
Huh?

00:20:22.650 --> 00:20:25.750
Every single time, we got transported to these weird worlds...

00:20:25.750 --> 00:20:27.310
...but it was all 'cause of you, wasn't it?!

00:20:27.590 --> 00:20:29.830
Ah-ha, I see.

00:20:30.320 --> 00:20:32.030
This is no time to be impressed!

00:20:32.030 --> 00:20:34.330
Do you realize how much trouble you've put us through?!

00:20:35.100 --> 00:20:37.060
I know what you're saying, but...

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:38.300
What?

00:20:38.300 --> 00:20:41.860
If we go back to the original Abenobashi, you're gonna move away, right?

00:20:42.070 --> 00:20:42.840
So, what about it?

00:20:43.270 --> 00:20:45.760
But we won't be able to see each other anymore...

00:20:46.410 --> 00:20:48.610
What the heck? That can't be helped!

00:20:48.610 --> 00:20:49.390
Can't be helped?

00:20:50.080 --> 00:20:52.070
Arumi, you're okay with that?

00:20:52.180 --> 00:20:53.980
Well, sure, I'm a little sad about it...

00:20:53.980 --> 00:20:55.920
...but it's already been decided.

00:20:56.150 --> 00:20:57.220
But you know...

00:20:57.220 --> 00:20:58.980
Don't sulk so blatantly!

00:20:59.450 --> 00:21:02.650
Then, you're okay with being in these worlds forever?

00:21:02.820 --> 00:21:03.890
These messed up worlds...

00:21:03.890 --> 00:21:05.690
...where you don't even know what's going to happen tomorrow?

00:21:05.690 --> 00:21:08.460
That's not exactly what I meant, but...

00:21:08.460 --> 00:21:11.520
Well, if we're talking about if that kinda thing is totally bad...

00:21:11.630 --> 00:21:13.430
...I think it's got its own...

00:21:13.430 --> 00:21:14.330
Make up your mind!

00:21:14.840 --> 00:21:17.580
There's no point in being in these places forever, right?

00:21:17.940 --> 00:21:18.970
You think so?

00:21:18.970 --> 00:21:20.090
Don't consider it!

00:21:21.510 --> 00:21:24.850
I want to go back to the world where everyone is normal.

00:21:24.850 --> 00:21:27.280
And that's where I want to think about my family and my friends...

00:21:27.260 --> 00:21:29.510
...and about you, Sasshi.

00:21:29.850 --> 00:21:31.680
Come on, let's go home.

00:21:33.150 --> 00:21:34.190
Yeah.

00:21:34.190 --> 00:21:35.560
Okay, I got it!

00:21:35.560 --> 00:21:37.180
You're really something Arumi.

00:21:37.620 --> 00:21:41.290
This time, I'll make sure to only think about getting home.

00:21:41.660 --> 00:21:42.720
Sasshi...

00:21:43.030 --> 00:21:44.360
Well, are you ready?

00:21:50.040 --> 00:21:51.790
All things extant in this world...

00:21:52.140 --> 00:21:55.230
...gods of Heaven, gods of Earth, let them be as they should be.

00:21:55.780 --> 00:21:57.330
All things extant in this world...

00:21:57.780 --> 00:22:00.540
...gods of Heaven, gods of Earth, let them be as they should be.

00:22:01.220 --> 00:22:02.770
All things extant in this world...

00:22:03.120 --> 00:22:05.880
...gods of Heaven, gods of Earth, let them be as they should be.

00:22:06.520 --> 00:22:08.010
Thus shall it be.

00:23:46.150 --> 00:23:49.420
Let's see, next time on Abenobashi...

00:23:47.750 --> 00:23:49.420
You better knock it off already!

00:23:49.420 --> 00:23:52.130
We got sent to stupid worlds every time, and it was all your fault!

00:23:52.130 --> 00:23:53.590
Yeah, who would've thought?

00:23:53.590 --> 00:23:55.800
This is no time to be impressed! This is your problem too!

00:23:55.800 --> 00:23:57.600
Now, now, it's all behind us now.

00:23:57.600 --> 00:23:58.670
Anyway, about the next episode...

00:23:58.670 --> 00:24:00.570
No, you're not getting off that easy.

00:24:00.570 --> 00:24:03.040
But it wasn't like I was doing it on purpose.

00:24:03.040 --> 00:24:05.170
So, you can do anything as long as it's not on purpose?

00:24:05.170 --> 00:24:06.270
Quit being so childish.

00:24:06.270 --> 00:24:07.270
I am a child.

00:24:07.270 --> 00:24:08.910
At any rate, the preview for next week...

00:24:08.910 --> 00:24:10.640
No! I'm mad, so I'm not gonna let you do it!

00:24:10.640 --> 00:24:12.350
No way! I'm gonna do the preview!

00:24:13.010 --> 00:24:14.880
Next time on Magical Shopping Arcade Abenobashi...
